# Lettre de motivation, Ripple and Roll, TA Stylised Environments (7 October 2026)

Base : la lettre Drama Studios du 7 October 2026, en anglais, version freelance. Objet du mail : TA Stylised Environments. (7 October 2026)

## English (7 October 2026)

Subject: TA Stylised Environments

To the recruitment team,

Hello Ripple and Roll,

I am writing about your opening for Technical Artist, Stylised Rendering [Environments].

"Where others add geometry, you add a shader": that line describes exactly how I like to work, and it is what made me write to you.

My name is Matthieu Huguet, I am 25 and I work as a freelance Technical Artist, based in Aix-en-Provence, France.

I studied a Game Design Bachelor at LISAA Paris, a Master's at ARTFX Montpellier, then technical art courses at Gnomon and through Harvard CS50, before going freelance in early 2025.

I worked on 2 NDA projects with Meerkat Studio and on an archviz project for a private client in Aix-en-Provence since 2025. All my work can be seen at matthieuhuguet.com.

Right now I am working on integrating and building solutions with Houdini and Unreal that generate level design through HDAs and let me iterate on it quickly. My latest published work: Fleur de Lys, Procedural Lily, Ceramic Tiles and HDA Stairs Component.

Your opening for Technical Artist, Stylised Rendering lines up with my day-to-day work: Houdini, procedural shading and textures, and environment assets built to be reused by other artists.

What I am looking for today is a mission with a team committed to an ambitious project. I need to work with experienced professionals and be part of a collective dynamic, something that working solo, however formative, cannot provide.

I am available to start right away, remotely, as a freelancer invoicing from France. My CV is attached.

I would be happy to talk with you by phone or video call, whenever suits you.

Matthieu Huguet
